// Title: Potential DLL Sideloading Via ClassicExplorer32.dll
// Sigma ID: caa02837-f659-466f-bca6-48bde2826ab4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-12-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL sideloading using ClassicExplorer32.dll from the Classic Shell software
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blogs.blackberry.com/en/2022/12/mustang-panda-uses-the-russian-ukrainian-war-to-attack-europe-and-asia-pacific-targets
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/6d8cabb0-dcda-44b6-8050-28d6ce281687/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_classicexplorer32.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ClassicExplorer32.dll" and (not(FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Classic Shell\\"))
